fof_version: '1.0'
type: enemy
id: the_wept
name: The Wept
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 1.0.0
enemy:
  level: 6
  role: boss
  armor: 2                # not armor: wrongness. Blades land and matter less than they should
  morale: 12              # fearless
  weapon: "Bare hands, and strength like a fact"
  wants: >
    Raunu Boranis, on the dais, and nothing else until that is done. It has a
    task, not a body count.
  special: >
    UNDEFEATABLE — the Wept cannot be beaten by force tonight. At 0 HP it is
    not defeated: it stops indulging the interference, puts whoever struck the
    last blow through a wall (they drop to 0 HP and are out of the scene), steps
    into the world's shadow, and returns the next exchange at full HP, resuming
    its task. A player character it drops to 0 HP takes the Wound, but Hold On
    can go no lower than 7–9: out of the fight, conscious, never dying. It has
    no orders about them, and no appetite. THE LEASH — from the first scream it
    has roughly half an hour of story-time; when the last bell of Oraga rings,
    it leaves, finished or not.
  when_bloodied: >
    The Sorrow Slips. The mask's carved tears begin to run — actually run. Its
    10+ hits land as 7–9 hits (no extra damage), it hums the cradle-song
    mid-attack without knowing, and its Fracture drops to Standard whatever
    tells have been seen. It is losing the argument with what it used to be.
  tells: >
    FRACTURE TELLS, each worth ammunition (one tell: the Fracture is Hard; two
    or more: Standard). Before midnight: watches the young pages at the feast a
    beat too long; leaves a mourner's offering in Elanna's niche in a rite
    centuries out of date; lingers at the east wing doors humming a cradle-song
    no one living knows; tells a dance partner, kindly, "You dance like my
    daughter would have." During the attack: goes still at the sound of a child
    crying; under the carved tears, the mask is a woman's face. In a fight, it
    does not wind up — it arrives, and whoever is between it and the dais is
    the target.
  breaks: >
    Morale never breaks it. What morale cannot do, its Fracture does. FRACTURE —
    SORROW (once): a Soul roll, requiring ammunition gathered in play. On a
    10+ the Wept stops — mid-motion, mid-kill — and for one full exchange it is
    a person standing in a burning ballroom. On a 7–9 it stops, but answers
    first with one terrible parting blow (the MM rolls it in the open) or word.
  twists:
  - "A ward flares between it and the dais; it goes around, and the long way costs it an exchange."
  - "A crystal charge in a player character's hand goes cold and dark."
  - "It steps through the world's shadow and is suddenly on the other side of the party."
  - "A guest falls in its path; it steps around them without looking, and everyone sees it do so."
  - "It pauses at a child's cry from somewhere in the palace. That is a tell."
  - "The leash tugs. It looks east for a heartbeat, and is faster afterward."
  nastier: >
    Late in the attack it grows faster, sloppier, and more human: after the
    party's third exchange against it, it attacks three times an exchange, and
    every hit it lands is loud with grief.
  description: >
    The tallest of the three gray masks: a spirit-mask carved with falling
    tears, warm sure hands, and the manners of a court two centuries gone. She
    is a person — that is the thing to hold onto — a woman, gracious and
    quietly sad, who praised the wine and danced beautifully. She leads. She
    goes for Raunu Boranis and she does not hurry, because nothing at this
    ball can stop her, and she knows exactly what that feels like from the
    other side.

    She watched the young pages at the feast a beat too long. She left a
    mourner's offering in Elanna's niche, in a rite centuries out of date. She
    lingered at the nursery doors humming a cradle-song no one living knows,
    and told a dance partner, kindly, "You dance like my daughter would have."
    Under the carved tears, the mask is a woman's face.
  notes: >
    THE TRUTH behind the Fracture: she was a mother; disease took her family
    while she stood helpless; tonight she has been sent to inflict on a family
    what the world inflicted on hers.

    SHADOW-STEP: it slips through the world's shadow — short relocations that
    read as arriving rather than running. Ordinary doors, walls, and barricades
    do not reliably hold it; deep Boranis ward-crystal does.

    UNRAVELING PRESENCE: within a stone's throw, a released crystal charge
    works only on a Soul roll at Standard; on a 6− the charge dies dark. The
    palace's great wards hold longer but gutter at close range.

    FORCE BUYS TIME: fighting it never ends in victory, but every exchange
    spent on a stubborn defender is a hallway Veier gains, a dozen guests out
    the service doors, a ward resealed. Make the cost honest and the purchase
    visible. Only ward-fire, the leash, and its Fracture change outcomes. See
    module Chapter V, "You Cannot Beat Them."
  organization: >
    One of three. The others hold the doors and the Dance while it works the
    dais.
  reskin_of: null
created_at: '2026-07-12T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-09-25T00:00:00+00:00'
